language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Maximum density still life: a stable pattern of live cells on an n x m grid, maximising the number of live cells.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(1..)
$ the active grid is padded with two rings of dead cells so every neighbour index is in range
find P : matrix indexed by [int(0..n+3), int(0..m+3)] of bool
$ the output grid is the active n x m area of the padded board
find grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..m)] of bool

branching on [grid]
maximising (sum i : int(1..n) . sum j : int(1..m) . toInt(grid[i,j]))
such that
$ the cells outside the padded area and in the outer ring are dead
forAll c : int(0..m+3) . (P[0,c] = false /\ P[1,c] = false /\ P[n+2,c] = false /\ P[n+3,c] = false),
forAll r : int(2..n+1) . (P[r,0] = false /\ P[r,1] = false /\ P[r,m+2] = false /\ P[r,m+3] = false),
$ the output grid is the active area of the padded board
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll j : int(1..m) . (grid[i,j] = P[i+1,j+1]),
$ a live cell must have exactly 2 or 3 live neighbours to remain alive
forAll r : int(1..n+2) . forAll c : int(1..m+2) . (P[r,c] -> (((toInt(P[r-1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r-1,c]) + toInt(P[r-1,c+1]) + toInt(P[r,c-1]) + toInt(P[r,c+1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c]) + toInt(P[r+1,c+1])) = 2) \/ ((toInt(P[r-1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r-1,c]) + toInt(P[r-1,c+1]) + toInt(P[r,c-1]) + toInt(P[r,c+1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c]) + toInt(P[r+1,c+1])) = 3))),
$ a dead cell, including any dead cell just outside the active grid, must not have exactly 3 live neighbours
forAll r : int(1..n+2) . forAll c : int(1..m+2) . ((!P[r,c]) -> ((toInt(P[r-1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r-1,c]) + toInt(P[r-1,c+1]) + toInt(P[r,c-1]) + toInt(P[r,c+1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c-1]) + toInt(P[r+1,c]) + toInt(P[r+1,c+1])) != 3))
